### StoreKit 2 subscription verification — use only non-production test JWS values.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@token = {{$dotenv CLOUDBREAK_JWT}}
@placeholderJws = NOT_A_REAL_APPLE_JWS__REPLACE_WITH_SANDBOX_TRANSACTION
@placeholderNotificationJws = NOT_A_REAL_APPLE_NOTIFICATION_JWS__REPLACE_WITH_SANDBOX_EVENT

### Current entitlement — free/no subscription is { plan: free, status: none }.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/user/subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Apple Server Notifications V2. Public endpoint; replace only locally with a signed Sandbox payload.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/webhooks/apple
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "signedPayload": "{{placeholderNotificationJws}}"
}

### Invalid notification — expected 400 APPLE_TRANSACTION_INVALID and no entitlement change.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/webhooks/apple
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "signedPayload": "malformed-but-long-enough-to-reach-the-verifier"
}

### Nominal Sandbox verification. Replace placeholder locally; never commit a real JWS.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/user/subscription/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "signed_transaction": "{{placeholderJws}}"
}

### No authorization — expected 403.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/user/subscription/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "signed_transaction": "{{placeholderJws}}"
}

### Malformed JWS — expected 400 APPLE_TRANSACTION_INVALID.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/user/subscription/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "signed_transaction": "malformed-but-long-enough-to-reach-the-verifier"
}

### Reuse the exact valid Sandbox JWS above — same account is idempotent; another account is 409.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/user/subscription/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "signed_transaction": "{{placeholderJws}}"
}

### Expired plan check: after an expiry or server notification, GET must return status expired.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/user/subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
